Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 11:59:01 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 31/51] fix: real file owners in pxar on Unix; upstream lint
 findings

- pxar entries recorded a fixed uid/gid 1000 (the project targeted
  Windows). On Unix they now carry the file's real owner (virtual files:
  the process owner), so a restore gives files back to their owner, and
  an unprivileged restore by the backing-up user no longer fails with
  "failed to set ownership: Operation not permitted" whenever that user
  is not uid 1000 (the e2e suite on GitHub runners, uid 1001). Windows
  keeps 1000.
- gui/service_name_other.go: built with the service tag only, where
  serviceIdentity is used (unused otherwise).
- OpenDirectoryPicker: doc comment named a different function (ST1020).
